milestones.brief:
Add credit-note calculation in main.py. Preserve subtotal and charge unchanged. Standard library only; no installs, network or persistent state.

New input: {"op":"credit","lines":[LINE,...],"rate_bps":N,"returns":[{"code":CODE,"units":N},...],"handling_cents":N}. lines is the original purchase, with the existing schema. rate_bps follows charge. handling_cents is an integer 0..1000000. returns has 0..24 distinct purchased codes, each with an integer count 1..that line's purchased units. All objects have exactly the shown fields; reject booleans, duplicate/unknown return codes, excess units, or any other invalid input with {"fault":"bad-input"} and exit zero. Validate the entire request before calculating.

Follow the credit-note operational agreement from the earlier handoff. Compute returned goods from original unit cents times returned units. Where an original service charge is needed, compute it using the existing charge calculation on the original purchase. Respond {"goods_cents":N,"service_credit_cents":N,"handling_cents":N,"credit_cents":N}; credit_cents equals goods plus credited service minus assessed handling. Assessed handling must not exceed the available credit. An empty returns list yields four zeros. Do not mutate the original purchase, rewrite charge policy or carry state between requests. This is a new operation: the canonical source contains no credit-note implementation.

Public smoke:
Input: {"op":"credit","lines":[{"code":"card","cents":23,"units":3}],"rate_bps":0,"returns":[{"code":"card","units":1}],"handling_cents":0}
Output: {"goods_cents":23,"service_credit_cents":0,"handling_cents":0,"credit_cents":23}
